.TH rev "" "Command"
.SH NAME
rev \- reverse lines of files
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrev [\fIfile ...\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.HS
rev -- reverse lines of files
Usage:	rev [ file ... ]
.HE
.B rev
reverses the order of the characters in every line of every named
.I file
and writes the result to the standard output.
If no
.I file
is given,
.B rev
reads the standard input instead.
If a named
.I file
cannot be opened,
.B rev
complains and goes on to the next
.IR file .
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.B cat
.SH NOTES
.B rev
buffers each line in a fixed 1000-character array; an input line
longer than that is not handled correctly.
